<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Exclusions must earn their place. Each one states what the detector is
    protecting against and why that threat cannot reach this code, so a future
    reader can check the claim rather than trust it. Nothing is excluded here
    that has not first been seen to fire.
-->
<FindBugsFilter>

    <!--
        EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2 in the entity package: an object that hands
        out a reference to mutable state lets a caller change it from outside.

        In an entity that reference is the point. `member.getHousehold()` returns
        the household row this member belongs to, and returning a copy would hand
        back an object Hibernate does not manage: writes to it would never reach
        the database, and `==` against the same row loaded elsewhere in the
        persistence context would be false. The identity is the association.

        The detector cannot tell an entity reference from a mutable value, so the
        exclusion is scoped to the package rather than to the two methods. What
        makes that safe is a check that can be run rather than trusted: every
        field in this package is a Long, a String, an Instant or another entity,
        and no getter returns a collection. A collection getter that appears here
        later must return a copy, and a mutable value type must not be added at
        all, because this exclusion would hide both.

        Scoped to entities deliberately. A controller or service that leaks
        mutable state is still worth a look, which is why this names one package
        instead of the whole application. A second entity package gets its own
        entry here only after the check above has been run against it.

        Seen to fire on 2026-09-22: Member.getHousehold and Member.setHousehold,
        2 bugs, build failed. Removing this block reproduces that.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Package name="se.teaterihuskvarna.member"/>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>

</FindBugsFilter>
